From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: honour the configured TX power

The power target was capped only by the SROM and the regulatory limit of
the channel, so a lower TX power set from user space had no effect. Cap
it by the power mac80211 configures as well, with the antenna gain
taken off as for the regulatory limit.

Index: backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
===================================================================
--- backports-7.2.orig/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
+++ backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
@@ -1948,6 +1948,19 @@
 			best = lim;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The configured TX power, which mac80211 has already capped to the
+	 * channel's limit, so it is in the same units as max_power.
+	 */
+	if (dev->phy.desired_txpower > 0) {
+		int lim = B43_PHY_AC_QDB(dev->phy.desired_txpower) - antgain;
+
+		if (lim < 0)
+			lim = 0;
+		if (lim < best)
+			best = lim;
+	}
+
 	{
 		u16 locale = b43_phy_ac_locale_ceiling(ac);
 
